385	1139,943,1742,1813 - 1150,1295,1300,1505 - 1566,1590,1760,1813	385. Dwarf Cornel.	A Dwarf Cornel plant: a creeping woody stem with rootlets sending up a stalk that ends in a whorl of veiny leaves and a flower-head framed by four broad white involucre-leaves.
387	1160,1332,1292,1501	387. A fruit cut across.	The berry-like stone-fruit with its top sliced off, showing the two cells of the stone side by side.
386	1566,1612,1742,1793	386. A separate flower enlarged.	One small flower enlarged, with four pointed petals spread open, four stamens and a central style rising from the top of the ovary.
